# ── Secrets — never commit. Treat git history as public from commit one. ────
.env
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

# ── Dependencies / build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/

# ── Runtime logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log

# ── Installed skills (third-party — reinstallable via `npx skills add ...`,
#    not our source). Also removes their bundled .md files (README.md,
#    SKILL.md, reference/*.md, etc.) from consideration before the repo-root
#    .md rule below even applies. ────────────────────────────────────────────
.agents/
.claude/

# ── Project docs: README.md is tracked, every other root-level .md is not
#    (ARCHITECTURE.md, STRATEGY.md, RULES.md). Anchored to the repo root
#    (leading "/") so this never reaches into node_modules/ or the skill
#    directories above — both already fully ignored regardless. ────────────
/*.md
!/README.md
